course: dictionary
lesson: 8342
title: A name in a sentence
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Ron is a name. A name tells you who a sentence is about, and it starts with a capital letter. Ron is often short for Ronald.
explain: In a maths word problem, Ron is usually a made-up person in a story. Ask yourself who has, buys, gives or earns something. «Ron has 12 marbles and gives away 4» tells you Ron is the person who has the marbles.
explain: In everyday life, Ron is a common name in English-speaking countries. «Grandad Ron has a nicotine patch on his arm» tells you Ron is a grandad, a person in the story. Look at the words around a name to find out who it is.
fact: A name starts with a capital letter, so «Ron» always has a big R.
fact: «Ron» is a boy's or man's name, often short for Ronald.
fact: «Ron Weasley» is a famous friend of Harry Potter in books and films.
fact: In maths, Ron is a person in a story who has, buys, gives or earns something.
fact: Ron is a common name in English-speaking countries.
exercise: In maths: «Ron has 12 marbles and gives away 4.» Who is Ron in this problem? | A town in Scotland | *A person in the story who has the marbles | A type of marble | A kind of sum
exercise: «Ron Weasley is a famous friend of Harry Potter.» What kind of name is Ron here? | A name of a character in books and films | *A character in books and films | A food | A colour
exercise: Find and copy one word that is a person's name: «Grandad Ron has a nicotine patch on his arm.» | *Ron | arm | nicotine | patch
test: «Ron» is often short for which name? | Rebecca | *Ronald | Rhoda
test: In «Austin's Butterfly», who is Ron Berger? | A classmate who gave feedback | A butterfly | *A teacher who tells the story | A young boy who drew six drafts
exam: Why is Ron written with a capital R in «Grandad Ron has a nicotine patch on his arm»? | It is a very important word | It is the first word in the sentence | *It is a name, and names start with a capital letter | It is a long word
